          "text": "Mr. MORRILL. I move to reduce it to forty-nine, for the purpose of saying that the committee raised the duty from forty to fifty per cent, for the reason that we have raised the duty on iron from the present rates. I hope it will be allowed to remain as we have reported it. The gentleman from Ohio says that New York importers declare our existing tariff is prohibitory, when the fact is we have received under it this last year over $169,000,000 in revenue, which contradicts the declaration. I withdraw my amendment.",
